's documented correspondence to Node.\", \"Unique request contexts, ReadOnlySafe, no process or storage crash.\"], \"excluded\": [\"Unconditional public ReadIndex completion; requests can be lost per API.\", \"A time bound or general liveness result.\", \"Linearizability violation, lease-based reads, concurrent context reuse and joint-configuration exhaustive coverage.\"], \"parameters\": {}}, \"rationale\": \"Register an independent request-lifecycle question from the actual configuration commit path, preserving the early-Advance documentation tension and lossy public read contract.\", \"status\": \"pending\", \"previous_id\": null, \"version\": 1, \"boundary_changes\": [], \"obligation_checks\": {}, \"remaining_obligation_ids\": [\"C_read_gate_release\"], \"recheck_reasons\": [], \"semantic_readiness\": {}, \"coverage_limitations\": [\"No executable trigger requirement covers reference F_read_wait\", \"No executable trigger requirement covers reference B_read_wait\", \"No executable trigger requirement covers reference B_read_release\"], \"record\": {\"path\": \"state.json\", \"collection\": \"units\", \"match\": {\"id\": \"unit-C_read_gate_release\", \"version\": 1}}}]\nreview_issues []\ncurrent {\"phase\": \"executed\", \"operation_id\": \"e0ecf66107184976a84634f67fe70be6\", \"action\": \"obligation\"}\nlatest handoff {\"operation_id\": \"e0ecf66107184976a84634f67fe70be6\", \"action\": \"obligation\", \"candidate_ids\": [\"d1d723bef7bf4028982446cb269f188e\"], \"answered_preview\": \"Trusted exploration reached actual configuration-driven first-current-term commit: commit 6 -> 7 with the retained queue still containing one request; fresh read returned while the old request remained, and a later proposal advanced commit \\u2026\", \"ref_ids\": [\"cfa40e9c46064645aa6322f0a0286660\", \"S_early_advance_usage\", \"S_early_advance_readme\", \"S_node_advance_order\", \"S_raw_advance_contract\", \"S_pending_read_purpose\", \"S_read_api_contract\"], \"record\": {\"path\": \"state.json\", \"collection\": \"selections\", \"match\": {\"operation_id\": \"e0ecf66107184976a84634f67fe70be6\"}}, \"feedback\": {\"ref_ids\": [\"cfa40e9c46064645aa6322f0a0286660\", \"S_early_advance_usage\", \"S_early_advance_readme\", \"S_node_advance_order\", \"S_raw_advance_contract\", \"S_pending_read_purpose\", \"S_read_api_contract\"], \"answered\": \"Trusted exploration reached actual configuration-driven first-current-term commit: commit 6 -> 7 with the retained queue still containing one request; fresh read returned while the old request remained, and a later proposal advanced commit to 8 and released it. This is attributed exploration, not formal property Evidence. Package usage explicitly permits Advance after persistence before application; application order was preserved. The more restrictive RawNode shorthand remains a documented interpretation issue rather than being erased.\", \"remaining\": [\"Run and review a direct comparison for the narrowly sourced queue-transition contract.\", \"Resolve applicability in review using both the explicit early-Advance permission and the RawNode wording; retain any contrary interpretation.\"], \"understanding\": \"updated\", \"rationale\": \"The actual path replaces producer and prefix assumptions and makes a bounded local obligation worth checking. The public loss allowance prevents escalation to unconditional read liveness. This independent Candidate neither reopens nor strengthens the completed asynchronous stale-completion result.\", \"question_updates\": {}}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
